{ "Identifier":       {"ImplementerID": "1", "ImplementationID": "MMC-SIR-V2.5-I01", "AIMName": "MMC-SIR-V2.5"},

  "APIProfile":       "Basic",
  "Description":      "Speaker Identity Recognition: receives a Basic Speech Object, its Speech Time and the Basic Audio Scene Descriptors the speech was isolated from, matches the speaker against the Subject Gallery held in Shared Storage, and returns the speaker identity as an Instance Identifier. The scene descriptors are the audio counterpart of the visual scene context Face Identity Recognition receives: where several speakers are present, they place the speech within the scene it came from. They are optional, as the scene context is for the face: a Speech Object captured directly from a microphone has no scene to be placed in.",

